Package: nova-server
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-cryptography, qrencode, iproute2, systemd
Recommends: docker.io | docker-ce, ufw
Suggests: tailscale, cloudflared
Maintainer: Nova contributors <nova@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/
Description: secure phone & web remote for your home server
 Nova lets you manage a Linux home server from the Nova Android app or a
 browser: status and live graphs, containers (logs, shell, start/stop), an app
 store, drives, backups, alerts and an SSH terminal.
 .
 Every request is signed by a hardware-backed key on your phone; risky actions
 need your fingerprint. The API runs unprivileged in a systemd sandbox, and the
 only privileged code is a root helper with a fixed list of commands.
 .
 After installing, run:  sudo nova-setup
